# Radar UI

## Two draw paths

| Function | When | Behavior |
|----------|------|----------|
| `radarDisplayDraw()` | First paint, range change | Full static grid (rings, cardinals, scale label) |
| `radarDisplayRefreshAircraft()` | ADS-B update | Redraw aircraft on cached sprite — **no full-screen clear** |

Rendering uses a sprite frame buffer (`LGFX_Sprite s_frame` in `radar_display.cpp`).

## Range math

- Ring 3 label = ¾ of outer radius: `outer_km = ring3_km × 4/3`
- Presets in `kRangePresets[]`: 5, 10, 15, 25 km (default index 1 = 10 km)
- ADS-B fetch radius: `fetchRadiusKm()` scales outer_km to screen edge so rim bearing dots have data

## Aircraft display rules

- **Inside outer ring**: red nose triangle, magenta speed vector, callsign/type/alt tags
- **Beyond ring**: small red dot on screen rim at correct bearing (direction cue only)
- **Tags**: placed toward center — west aircraft get tags on the right, east on the left

## Constants belong in theme

Layout, colors, stroke widths, label sizes → `include/ui/radar_theme.h`. Do not inline magic pixel values in draw code.

RGB565 palette is initialized from theme byte targets (`kBgR`, `kGridG`, etc.) — avoid hardcoded color hex in draw functions.
